meta {
  name: Repeat Sample
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/repeat
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "repeatReason": "Sample clotted"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200); });
}

docs {
  Flag a sample for re-collection (REPEAT) with a mandatory reason.

  Not allowed from the sender once the sample is SENT_INTERNAL (422
  SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH).

  On the RECEIVING branch's copy of a transferred sample (a sample created by an
  accepted internal transfer) the test is not repeated in place - it goes back to
  the sender: the copy is voided (soft-deleted, CANCELLED), the report(s) return to the
  sender, and the sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT. Allowed only
  while every report the copy serves is untouched (PENDING, no result values, notes,
  attachments, overall-result entries or Notes-section overrides); otherwise 422
  SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED. The copy is not in the response (it is voided).
  Internal branch transfer rules (manager flow 2026-09-29):
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER's Technician
    worklist hides its report (list, counts, detail, history, every write, the five
    secondary worklists, attachments, inventory usage, analyser results). It behaves
    as "Lab report not found" (404 LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND) for the sender.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.
}
